WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.003
The working loop.

2
00:00:01.283 --> 00:00:05.912
Here is the loop a working team runs, and the one this week’s lab makes concrete.

3
00:00:06.192 --> 00:00:10.181
Keep a labeled query set in the repository, versioned with the code.

4
00:00:10.461 --> 00:00:20.744
Measure each retriever alone, then the hybrid, then the hybrid plus a reranker, reporting recall@k, MRR, and nDCG with k and the query count.

5
00:00:21.024 --> 00:00:34.165
Pick the reranker (hosted, open, or LLM) by measured gain per unit of latency and cost on your data, and remember that a cheap open cross-encoder is a legitimate baseline for any paid option.

6
00:00:34.445 --> 00:00:39.907
Log what was retrieved for every production answer, and triage failures with the flowchart above.

7
00:00:40.187 --> 00:00:46.672
Then add every new failure to the labeled set, so the system can only get better at the things it once got wrong.
